  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 104.54 Wet meadow",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 104.54 “Wet meadow” means an herb-dominated jurisdictional area typically with non-woody vegetation less than 3 feet in height, saturated for long periods during the growing season, but seldom flooded, as determined using the federal classification method. Wet meadows develop on predominantly drier, poorly drained soils.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, #3, and #4 at Chapter heading for Env-Wt 100) #12801, eff 12-15-19; renumbered by #13945 (formerly Env-Wt 104.53)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt100.html"
